<!-- ============ THE ROAD ============ -->
<section class="road-band" id="s-road" data-node>
  <div class="road-art"><img src="{{A:bg-chart.jpg}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="road-grid">
      <figure class="shot rise" style="margin:0">
        <div class="phone"><img src="{{A:mk-chart.jpg}}" alt="The beta Star Chart: a climbing road of 260 missions with a reward rail beside it" loading="lazy"></div>
        <figcaption>The actual screen</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rise" style="margin:0">
        <div class="phone"><video width="400" height="712" data-src="{{V:worlds.mp4}}" poster="{{A:worlds-poster.jpg}}" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="A flight past forest, molten and wormhole worlds"></video></div>
        <figcaption>26 stages on one road</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="rise">
        <p class="kicker">The Star Chart</p>
        <h2>260 missions on one climbing road.</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px">Numbered 1 to 260, three stars each &mdash; 780 in all. Beta opens the whole chart: <b>260 missions &middot; all unlocked in beta</b>. The reward rail rides beside the road, so you see what a star buys before you go for it. Spill missions on the road ask for waves, Ore, and Depots; the first wave-20 clear is level 258.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ THE FITTING ROOM ============ -->
<section class="fit-band" id="s-fit" data-node>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hd rise">
      <p class="kicker">The Fitting Room</p>
      <h2>Thirty suits. Not one of them is a recolour.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Twenty ship in the live game today; the ones marked <b>Soon</b> are upcoming on the beta shelf. Pick one below &mdash; helmet, trail, and pal are built to match.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="case-grid">
        <div class="case rise" id="case">
          <span class="case-beam" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="case-floor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="case-cnr tl" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="case-cnr tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="case-cnr bl" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="case-cnr br" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="case-plate">Now showing</p>
          <div class="case-stage"><img id="caseImg" alt=""></div>
          <p class="case-name"><b id="caseName">Seraph</b><span>Suit &middot; matching helmet &middot; trail</span></p>
        </div>
      <figure class="shot rise" style="margin:0">
        <div class="phone"><video width="400" height="712" data-src="{{V:squad.mp4}}" poster="{{A:squad-poster.jpg}}" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="A crew of squirrels in different suits flying together"></video></div>
        <figcaption>The whole crew, suited</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rise" style="margin:0">
        <div class="phone"><img src="{{A:mk-shop.jpg}}" alt="The Acornaut shop: a display case above shelves of suits, helmets and pals, with a running combo price" loading="lazy"></div>
        <figcaption>The shop, in the game</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="wall rise">
      <div class="rail" id="railA"><div class="rail-in" id="railAin"></div></div>
      <div class="rail rev" id="railB"><div class="rail-in" id="railBin"></div></div>
      <p class="tiny" style="margin-top:16px;text-align:center">30 on the wall &middot; 20 live &middot; 10 upcoming</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ STRAIGHT ANSWERS ============ -->
<section class="ans-band" id="s-ans" data-node>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hd rise">
      <p class="kicker">Before you ask</p>
      <h2>What it costs, what it isn't, who made it.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ans rise">
      <div>
        <h3>What does it cost?</h3>
        <p>Nothing to play. There is a shop, and it is built to be easy to ignore: the shelf restocks each day, anything you already own leaves it for good instead of being dangled at you, and one featured pack sits at half price. Everything on that shelf is a suit, a helmet, a trail or a pal.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Do I need an account?</h3>
        <p>No. No sign-in, no email, no download. Your progress lives in the browser you play it in.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Who made it?</h3>
        <p>One person. Every suit, planet and animation frame in it was painted for this game and nothing else.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CLOSE ============ -->
<section class="close">
  <div class="hero-art"><img src="{{A:bg-wide.jpg}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker" style="justify-content:center">One more thing</p>
    <h2>You have now read more about this game than it takes to play it.</h2>
    <a class="btn" href="https://acornaut.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="margin-top:14px">Play Acornaut</a>
    <p class="note" style="text-align:center">Free. No account.</p>
  </div>
</section>

